    "body": "@domenic You mean http://w3c-test.org/submissions/4089/workers/Worker_ErrorEvent_after_navigation.htm ?\n\nI see it report PASS twice in Chrome.  That said, the test seems to be asserting that the onerror of the window _after_ navigation never fires?  Why _would_ it fire?  I'm not quite sure what the test is trying to test....\n\nGithub is giving me a 500 error on https://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/pull/4089 as long as I'm signed in, so I guess I'll just put my other comments here:   You can presumably use assert_equals as `parent.assert_equals`, right?\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
